// M3-rtcall: the FIRST user .mid to call an EXPORTED runtime key.  The module
// header names it `RtCall` (every key is `RtCall.*`); its one defun `read`
// calls `Rt.read-file-as-string` — an EXPORTED runtime defun (runtime.mid's
// export block), so it resolves at J2 through the user lane's extern table
// (the privacy boundary: ONLY exported runtime keys resolve).  The call lowers
// to a RawCall naming `Rt.read-file-as-string`, which the emit level now
// SEEDS (grefsOf reports the RawCall-to-Rt edge, so `reach` pulls the Rt
// defun and its body's Rt->Rt closure into the emitted set) and calls in the
// callee's OWN ABI (an Rt key + rtLean => the lean 4-slot shape, the same
// shape lowerDefun emits for the callee).
module RtCall
export RtCall.read : val -> val
defun RtCall.read(path: val) -> val {
  return call Rt.read-file-as-string(path);
}
